{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ועשיתם אשה לה'", :translit "va'asitem isheh la'", :gloss "and you shall make a fire-offering to YHWH"} {:he "סמך פרשת נסכים למלחמה", :translit "samach parashat nesachim lamilchamah", :gloss "he juxtaposed the section of libations to war"} {:he "וכן בפנחס", :translit "vechen befinechas", :gloss "and likewise in Pinchas"} {:he "אשר יצא לפניהם", :translit "asher yetze lifneihem", :gloss "who goes out before them"} {:he "סמך מיד פרשת קרבנות", :translit "samach miyad parashat korbanot", :gloss "he juxtaposed immediately the section of sacrifices"} {:he "שבזכות הקרבנות היו נוצחים במלחמה", :translit "shebichut hakorbanot hayu notzachim bamilchamah", :gloss "for by merit of the sacrifices they were victorious in war"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut parshiyot: juxtaposition of adjacent sections yields a thematic lesson — libations/sacrifices adjacent to war-sections teach that offerings bring military victory"}], :frame {:text "The hermeneutical principle of semikhut parshiyot — deriving law or meaning from the Torah's placement of sections adjacent to one another — is treated as a valid mode of interpretation. The camp travels and wars with the ark going out before them, as stated in Numbers 10:35 'who goes out before them.' The Torah juxtaposes the section of libations (Numbers 15:1–16) immediately after the war narrative of the spies' rebellion and the ensuing decree that Israel would wander and fight (Numbers 14). Similarly in Numbers 28–29, the sacrificial section follows the war preparations. The Ba'al HaTurim reads both juxtapositions as teaching that sacrificial service secures victory in battle.", :sources ["Numbers 10:35" "Numbers 14" "Numbers 15:1-16" "Numbers 28-29"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut parshiyot: juxtaposition of adjacent sections yields a thematic lesson — libations/sacrifices adjacent to war-sections teach that offerings bring military victory", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:29:10.629081076Z", :model "glm-5.2"}